* ES-8 fixture: PROCESS SQL statement with opaque body (<<...>>)
* Valid Natural PROCESS SQL demonstrating:
* - DEFINE DATA LOCAL section with host variables
* - PROCESS SQL DDMNAME with multi-line opaque body
* - Literal :#PERS-ID inside << >> treated as opaque (unparsed)
* - Trailing CALLNAT after PROCESS SQL body parses successfully

DEFINE DATA LOCAL
  1 #PERS-ID (N9)
  1 #SALARY-PCT (P3.2)
END-DEFINE

PROCESS SQL DDMNAME
  << UPDATE SOME_TABLE
       SET SALARY = SALARY * 1.05
       WHERE PERS_ID = :#PERS-ID >>

CALLNAT 'NDBERR'

END
